THOUGHT 1: The detection call failed likely due to a transient remote error or trying to predict multiple diverse labels in one call. I'll make the code more robust: call detection for each label one-by-one inside try/except blocks so a failure for one label won't stop the rest, and if all direct detection calls fail I'll fall back to sliding_window_detection. I'll display any annotated outputs and print the returned boxes to help debug and continue the workflow.

ACTION 1:
```python
# python
labels = ["action figure", "toy", "rubber", "metal"]
successful_detections = {}
failed_labels = []

for lbl in labels:
    try:
        print(f"\nTrying detection for label: '{lbl}'")
        annotated_img, boxes = detection(image_1, [lbl])
        # detection may return None or raise; guard against None
        if annotated_img is None or boxes is None:
            raise RuntimeError(f"detection returned None for label '{lbl}'")
        display(annotated_img.annotated_image)
        print(f"Detected boxes for '{lbl}': {boxes}")
        successful_detections[lbl] = boxes
    except Exception as e:
        print(f"Detection failed for '{lbl}': {e}")
        failed_labels.append(lbl)

# If all single-label detections failed, try sliding window as a fallback
if len(successful_detections) == 0:
    try:
        print("\nAll single-label detections failed. Falling back to sliding_window_detection for combined search.")
        patches, patches_boxes = sliding_window_detection(image_1, labels)
        if not patches:
            print("sliding_window_detection returned no patches.")
        else:
            for i, patch in enumerate(patches):
                print(f"\nPatch {i+1}:")
                display(patch.annotated_image)
                print("Boxes in this patch:", patches_boxes[i])
    except Exception as e:
        print("sliding_window_detection also failed:", e)
else:
    print("\nAt least one label was detected. Proceeding with available detections.")
    print("Successful detections summary:", {k: successful_detections[k] for k in successful_detections})
